title: "Kepler: an open-source agent harness for ARC-AGI-3"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Wensen
    alias: Cveinnt
    email: contact@wensenwu.com
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cveinnt/kepler"
url: "https://kepler-harness.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Kepler is an open-source agent harness for ARC-AGI-3. Final boards:
  single-configuration 100.00 RHAE with Claude Opus 5 (v7, visual mode, all 25
  public games, every level at the efficiency cap) and 95.97 with GPT-5.6 Sol
  (v6, server-verified exact, 20.7M measured tokens). The model encodes its
  theory of each game as an executable world model, certifies it against the
  recorded interaction history, and a fail-closed mechanical replayer plays the
  scored attempt. Ships with append-only per-action ledgers for every run
  (failures included), adversarial audits, per-game token and action
  accounting, a CI-enforced zero-game-priors gate, and a controlled modality
  ablation. Public-set scores are not a measure of AGI progress; see the
  ARC-AGI-3 technical report.
keywords:
  - ARC-AGI-3
  - world models
  - LLM agents
  - benchmark reproduction
